Mouse endothelial cells (MECA32+) were abundantly observed in the transplanted kidney organoid graft as well as within the glomerulus-like structures (Fig.
3c
), which indicates that endothelial cells from the host mouse kidney had extensively infiltrated into the transplanted kidney organoids and formed a vascular network.

The transplanted kidney organoids were vascularized and survived in the transplanted graft at 2 weeks after UUO and transplantation (Fig.
7a
).
